  -> F is level with E: once a sensor keeps windowed host state, the
     reverse channel adds nothing measurable on this corpus.
  -> G alone is close to E: the windowed host state is doing nearly all
     of the work, and the per-flow forward features add little.

  This is a LOWER bound. TTL diversity, DNS query-name entropy and TLS
  fingerprint rarity need packet data this corpus does not carry.

